          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "هجرة (hijra) is built on the native Arabic root h-j-r, \"to leave, to cut off\" (Lane). Hijra is leaving one's land for another: migration."
            }
          ]
        },
